## Curated builds

Reviewed against patch 2.1.67 on 2026-05-13. The live patch is 2.2.16a, so these have not been re-read against it yet.

### Mid Zone Control (Mid)

- Items: Arcane Boots, Glowing Wand, Wishing Lantern, Blood Wings, Divine Glaive, Holy Crystal
- Core: Glowing Wand, Wishing Lantern, Blood Wings
- Emblem: Mage Emblem with Rupture, Wilderness Blessing, Lethal Ignition
- Battle spell: Flicker
- Flex: Magic Boots over Arcane Boots when Use when your team already has enough early damage and Vexana needs more frequent Deathly Grasp and Cursed Blast cycles.; Winter Crown over Holy Crystal when Use when one assassin or hard-engage combo can reach you before Blood Wings shield buys enough space.; Genius Wand over Holy Crystal when Use when your team has multiple magic damage dealers and stacked Magic Defense shred matters more than maximum late Magic Power.; Immortality over Holy Crystal when Use in late Lord defense when a single death ends the game and your damage is already enough to punish grouped entries.
- Total cost: 12060 gold

Default ranked mid build that turns Vexana's delayed zones and Eternal Guard pressure into burn, current-HP damage, shielded repositioning, and late penetration.

### Cooldown Frontline Control (Mid)

- Items: Magic Boots, Enchanted Talisman, Glowing Wand, Ice Queen Wand, Wishing Lantern, Divine Glaive
- Core: Enchanted Talisman, Glowing Wand, Ice Queen Wand
- Emblem: Mage Emblem with Inspire, Wilderness Blessing, Impure Rage
- Battle spell: Flicker
- Flex: Arcane Boots over Magic Boots when Use when the enemy mid and roamer are punishable early and flat Magic Penetration matters more than cooldown tempo.; Blood Wings over Ice Queen Wand when Use when the enemy is not walking out of your zones and you need shield value against poke or partial dive.; Holy Crystal over Ice Queen Wand when Use when your front line already supplies reliable slows or lockdown and Vexana can convert setup into heavier burst.; Genius Wand over Wishing Lantern when Use when your team stacks magic damage and repeated Eternal Guard hits can keep Magic Defense shred active through the fight.
- Total cost: 11090 gold

Sustained control setup for front-to-back games where Vexana must cast often, slow exits, and keep burn pressure on tanks around objectives.

### Anti-Dive Survival (Mid)

- Items: Tough Boots, Glowing Wand, Winter Crown, Blood Wings, Divine Glaive, Immortality
- Core: Glowing Wand, Winter Crown, Blood Wings
- Emblem: Mage Emblem with Rupture, Wilderness Blessing, Impure Rage
- Battle spell: Purify
- Flex: Wishing Lantern over Immortality when Use when the enemy dive is manageable and HP-stacking frontliners are the real reason fights are taking too long.; Holy Crystal over Immortality when Use when your team has reliable peel and Vexana can afford to turn the last slot back into damage.; Magic Boots over Tough Boots when Use when the enemy threatens burst more than chain control and Purify alone covers the important disable.; Ice Queen Wand over Immortality when Use when the dive enters through predictable paths and extra slow control helps your team punish the retreat.
- Total cost: 10850 gold

Defensive mid build for CC-heavy dive drafts where Vexana needs Purify, stasis, and layered survivability before her second cast decides the fight.

